  "_what": "Approximate country centroids, (latitude, longitude) in degrees.",
  "_why_here": "Cartography is design's, not the channel's. These are positions on a shared basemap rather than measurements, so they do not belong in a science payload. The one thing that would justify moving them to CRO is if we ever want the CROPLAND centroid rather than the country centroid, which ASAP's own geometry could give: Egypt's cropland sits on the Nile, not in the middle of the country. Until a dot is visibly wrong, the country centroid is honest enough at this scale.",
